@@ -0,0 +1,175 @@
+# ngspice 47 reference checkpoint
+
+ngspice 42 remains the historical reference for the existing implementation and
+regressions. Checkpoint 13 adds a separately built ngspice 47 reference, without
+changing neospice, fixtures, assertions or tolerances. Results from the two
+versions must not be combined into one compatibility percentage.
+
+This page's test table and corpus results describe historical checkpoint 13.
+Checkpoint 19 implements version 47's independent MES area/multiplier inputs.
+The complete 47 suite now has 1,202 passed and one failed out of 1,203, with no
+skips. RFF70N06 still fails. All nine unchanged MES noise fixtures now pass.
+See [current progress](joss-progress.md)
+and [transient diagnostics](transient-readiness.md); the historical margins
+below must not be quoted as current results.
+
+Both checkpoint 15 corpus runs have now completed and passed independent artifact
+audits. The version-47 run contains 67,359 fixture records and 649,749 verified
+artifact files. Its [summary](evidence/joss/2026-09-10-checkpoint15-corpus-run47-summary.json)
+and [paired reference transitions](evidence/joss/2026-09-10-checkpoint15-reference42-to47-transitions.json)
+retain all outcome categories. There are 1,214 changed labels between reference
+versions and no neospice reexecution differences. These runs use the frozen
+checkpoint 15 binary, before the MOS3 callback change; they are not a full-corpus
+validation of subsequent candidates.
+
+The scheduling change additionally fixes the constant-line time grid and the
+JFET2, MOS3 and VBIC transient comparisons against 47. The historical 42 suite
+now retains nine failures, including the scheduling differences, AC frequency
+grid, two AM-source comparisons and MES noise. The references remain separately labeled;
+no per-fixture reference substitution or tolerance change is used.
+
+The AM discrepancy traced in checkpoint 17 is a source-language incompatibility, not a small
+waveform error. Version 42 interprets `AM(1 0.5 10K 1MEG 0)` as amplitude 1,
+modulation offset 0.5, modulation frequency 10 kHz, carrier 1 MHz and delay zero.
+Version 47's `vsrcload.c` assigns those same fields to output offset, modulation
+offset, modulation amplitude, modulation frequency and carrier frequency. Its
+carrier is therefore zero and its output after time zero is constant 1 V.
+The new form also supports distinct modulation/carrier phases. Checkpoint 18
+implements the version-47 grammar in both source types, preserving explicit zero
+frequencies and resolving omitted frequencies for each transient duration. The
+original fixture and a new modulated voltage/current fixture pass against 47.
+See [migration guidance](source-compatibility.md) for existing netlists and C++
+parameters. Final release reference/CI policy remains pending.
+
+## Build and runtime
+
+The release archive and source inventory are pinned in the
+[acquisition record](evidence/joss/2026-09-10-ngspice47-acquisition.json).
+Its SHA-256 is
+`894e649651f1838a14095e5a5439e7d3aa63e87ede14d283173fda4fcdef675f`.
+The packaged configure script was used in separate build directories; the
+extracted source was not patched. Both configurations use:
+
+```sh
+/path/to/ngspice-47/configure --prefix=/path/to/install \
+  --without-x --with-readline=no --disable-debug CFLAGS='-O2 -g'
+make -j8
+make install
+```
+
+The shared-library configuration additionally uses `--with-ngshared`. XSPICE,
+KLU, OSDI and OpenMP are enabled by the release defaults. KLU being compiled in
+does not mean it is the selected solver: the default task uses Sparse, and the
+MES probes report `Using SPARSE 1.3 as Direct Linear Solver`. No KLU selection
+or numerical convergence option was added.
+
+The installed, unmodified `spinit` names the installed code models with absolute
+paths and disables its OSDI branch. It also sets **`num_threads=8`**. The runner's
+`OMP_NUM_THREADS=1` environment does not override that setting: ngspice's
+`CKTsetup` calls `omp_set_num_threads` with the frontend variable. Thus eight
+corpus workers may each request eight ngspice threads. This is a runtime
+difference from the historical installation and a limitation of the concurrent
+timeout experiment. These elapsed times are not performance benchmark samples.
+
+The C++ build uses the ngspice 47 pkg-config directory explicitly. `ldd` confirms
+that the test executables resolve the separately installed version-47 library.
+The earlier version-42 build and its evidence remain intact. The fresh build
+reuses the existing pinned GoogleTest source and cached RFF70N06 library; it is
+not an independent installation or clean-download reproduction.
+
+## C++ comparison results
+
+The complete Release suite has **1,183 tests: 1,173 passed, ten failed, no skips**.
+An earlier partial build left 20 device executables unbuilt; its failed CTest
+attempt is retained, but is not the full-suite result.
+
+| Failing test | Observed result with ngspice 47 |
+|---|---|
+| FrequencyGrid.MatchesNgspiceACAndNoiseRules | Sub-decade AC frequency grid differs. |
+| NgspiceCompareTest.RLCSeriesTransient | Maximum normalized error 0.0108912; tolerance 0.005. |
+| NgspiceCompareTest.ConstantTlineTimeGridMatchesNgspice | One asserted timestamp differs by approximately 14 ps. |
+| NgspiceCompareTest.AmSourceTransient | AM parameter interpretation differs; maximum normalized error 2.49987. |
+| RFF70N06.OriginalCorpusOperatingPoint | Reference itself aborts transient-OP fallback; neospice's historical failure remains unresolved. |
+| LTRAValidation.TransientRC | Source-current error 0.123542; tolerance 0.05. |
+| MesValidation.NoiseSpectraAcrossPolarityGeometryAndTemperature | MES M/AREA combinations have different reference semantics. |
+| JFET2Validation.NjfSwitchingTransient | Gate-current error 0.444640; tolerance 0.1. |
+| MOS3Validation.NmosTransientPulse | Drain-voltage error 0.0646054; tolerance 0.05. |
+| VBICValidation.SwitchingTransient | Collector-voltage error 1.47834; tolerance 0.27. |
+
+The six test names failing with ngspice 42 also fail here, though the RFF70N06
+failure occurs in the reference and several numerical margins differ. Four
+additional test names fail with 47. These are retained results requiring
+version-specific interpretation and supported-scope decisions, not skipped tests
+or justification for weakening assertions.
+
+## Confirmed reference differences
+
+* **Post-solve device convergence:** 42's `NIconvTest` returns the `OK` result
+  from `CKTconvTest` even when an individual tester sets `CKTnoncon`. `NIiter`
+  then assigns that zero back to the flag. Version 47 explicitly preserves the
+  device failure. Checkpoint 15 verifies the lost flag under gdb on the unchanged
+  RFF70N06 fixture. This qualifies 42's successful OP result and the interpretation
+  of historical comparisons; it does not remove the required regression.
+  Load-time device flags still operate in 42. See [RFF diagnostics](rff70n06-investigation.md).
+* **MES multiplier:** version 42 maps netlist `M` to `MES_AREA`; version 47 maps
+  it to `MES_M`, an independent multiplier. Direct shared-library probes run all
+  nine existing noise fixtures against both versions. All nine agree with
+  neospice against 42. Against 47, six agree, while `multiplier`, `scaled_hot`
+  and `area_last` have maximum normalized spectral errors approximately
+  0.178904, 1.34095 and 1.26545, respectively, at the unchanged 1e-8 tolerance.
+  The two combined AREA/M fixtures return effective area 7.5 with 47, versus
+  last-assignment values 3 and 2.5 with 42. The probes retain returned parameter
+  query values and diagnostics; they do not infer internal geometry solely from
+  a query name. Relevant source: `src/spicelib/devices/mes/{mes.c,mesparam.c,mesask.c}`.
+* **Sub-decade AC sweep:** 47 uses `exp(log(10)/points_per_decade)` when the
+  requested interval is less than one decade. Version 42 instead spaces a
+  floored number of steps over the requested interval. The existing `.ac dec
+  10 1 3` regression therefore has different coordinates. Relevant source:
+  `src/spicelib/analysis/acan.c`. This does not by itself establish noise-grid
+  behavior for every sweep mode.
+* **AM source:** 47 interprets the leading parameters as output offset,
+  modulation offset, modulation amplitude, modulation frequency and carrier
+  frequency. Version 42 interprets the corresponding fields differently.
+  In the unchanged `AM(1 0.5 10K 1MEG 0)` fixture, 47 has zero carrier frequency
+  and a constant 1 V after startup. Relevant source:
+  `src/spicelib/devices/vsrc/vsrcload.c`. Rewriting the reference fixture would
+  change the experiment rather than resolve version compatibility.
+
+The constant-line timestamp and nonlinear transient differences need further
+source-level investigation. No broad compatibility with every ngspice version
+is claimed, and the historical correctness blockers remain.
+
+## Limited reference sanitizer probes
+
+The standalone lifecycle reproducer was linked to ngspice 47 with AddressSanitizer
+and UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer enabled in the driver. All nine MES noise paths,
+the original `nmos_cs_amp_ac.cir` path and the original long BSIM4 diagnostic path
+completed with exit zero and no sanitizer reports, with leak detection enabled.
+The last two paths and `mes_noise_area.cir` had triggered version-42 filename
+buffer overflows. Execution took place outside ptrace so LeakSanitizer could run.
+
+The version-47 library itself is the ordinary Release build, not a fully
+instrumented library. These checks exercise the intercepted allocation/string
+paths; they do not certify all library memory accesses or resolve the 15 other
+historical reference-leak findings. The complete neospice sanitizer suite was
+not rerun in this checkpoint. Keep the version-42 findings visible.
+
+## Corpus experiment
+
+The same three predetermined smoke cases and all five planned variants were
+rerun. The two ordinary primary fixtures and one ordinary rescue match. Both
+RFF70N06 variants are `BOTH_FAIL`, whereas they were `NG_ONLY` with 42.
+Analytical divider and POLY runtime probes pass in both simulators.
+
+The completed 67,359-fixture version-47 run uses the unchanged checkpoint-11
+input manifest, checkpoint-12 runner and checkpoint-10 neospice binary. Primary
+and isolated/driven variants remain separate, with all failures retained.
+The [version-47 summary](evidence/joss/2026-09-10-corpus-run47-summary.json)
+retains all outcome categories. Primary fixtures have 20,224 MATCH, 1,277
+MISMATCH and 23 NG_ONLY; isolated/driven fixtures have 22,845 MATCH, 1,315
+MISMATCH and 52 NG_ONLY. Reference-failure categories remain in both denominators.
+The [version-transition report](evidence/joss/2026-09-10-reference42-to47-transitions.json)
+reconciles identical fixture bytes and neospice outputs across runs, with 1,214
+changed outcomes. This compares the declared runtime configurations, not an
+isolated ablation of one source-code change. Full-corpus results still require binding/dependency review and do not
+certify arbitrary analyses or independently resolved model definitions.
